@startuml inventory_sequence_diagram
title Machine Detail — Inventory Prefetch + Storage Scan + Clear Folders

actor User
participant "HomePresenter" as Presenter
participant "InventoryPresenter" as Detail
participant "ResolutionCoordinator" as Coord
participant "HostResolver" as Resolver
participant "InventoryService" as Inv
participant "DiskUsageService" as Disk
participant "AsyncJob" as Job
participant "RecentConnectionsStore" as Store

User -> Presenter: Select machine row
activate Presenter
Presenter -> Detail: SelectHost("PC-01")
activate Detail

group Prefetch IP (background)
    Presenter -> Resolver: NeedsResolve("PC-01")?
    Resolver --> Presenter: true (stale / unknown)
    Presenter -> Job: queue Resolve job
    note right of Coord: ResolutionCoordinator.CompleteResolve()\ncaches the IP and updates the row's\nreachability dot.
end

group Prefetch inventory (background, if stale)
    Detail -> Resolver: IsHostOnline + IsVerdictStale?
    note right of Detail: Only a FRESH 'Online' verdict gathers.\nOffline -> skipped; unknown/stale -> re-verified\noff-thread first (CompleteResolve re-gathers).
    Detail -> Detail: InventoryIsStale("PC-01")?
    Detail -> Inv: PrepareInventory("PC-01")
    Inv --> Detail: worker args (CIM probe script)
    Detail -> Job: queue Inventory job
    note right of Job: The worker tries a DCOM CIM session first\n(bounded 15s); the psexec probe is only\nthe fallback when CIM is unavailable/empty.
end
deactivate Presenter

== PumpJobs(): Inventory job completes -> CompleteInventory(job) ==
Detail -> Inv: ParseInventory("PC-01")
activate Inv
Inv --> Detail: MachineInventory (model, battery, disk, uptime)
deactivate Inv
Detail -> Store: UpsertInventory("PC-01", inv)
Detail -> Detail: PopulateDetailCards() -> HostViewModel.ApplyInventory()
note right of Detail: InventoryFormat derives battery-health,\ndisk-free and uptime labels (pure, tested);\nthe overview/detail bind to SelectedMachine.*.

== On demand ==
User -> Detail: Click "Storage scan" -> FindBigFolders("PC-01")
Detail -> Presenter: RequireElevation(DiskScan, "PC-01")
note right of Presenter: Elevation-gated: de-elevated, a pending\nintent is written + UAC relaunch; after the\nrestart ResumeDiskScan() re-enters here.\nSee elevation_sequence_diagram.puml.
Detail -> Disk: PrepareDiskScan("PC-01")
Disk --> Detail: worker args (TopN)
Detail -> Job: queue DiskScan job
note right of Detail: Worker deploys wiztree64.exe, MFT-scans C:,\ntrims the ranked export to the top rows on the target,\ncopies that small CSV back and caches top-N JSON.

== PumpJobs(): DiskScan job completes -> CompleteDiskScan(job) ==
Detail -> Disk: ParseDiskUsage("PC-01")
activate Disk
Disk --> Detail: DiskUsageReport (ranked folders)
deactivate Disk
Detail -> Store: UpsertDiskUsage("PC-01", report)
Detail -> Detail: HostViewModel.ApplyFolders(report)
note right of Detail: FolderNodeViewModel.FromReport() maps\nDiskUsageTree.BuildNested() to display nodes;\nthe TreeView binds SelectedMachine.Folders.

== On demand: clear checked folders ==
User -> Detail: "Clear selected" -> DeleteSelectedFolders("PC-01")
Detail -> Presenter: RequireElevation(DeleteFolders, "PC-01")
note right of Detail: Also elevation-gated, but NOT resumed after\nthe restart (the folder selection lives in this\nwindow) - the user re-picks. Confirmed via\nDialogPresenter before anything runs.
Detail -> Disk: PrepareDeleteFolders("PC-01", paths)
Disk --> Detail: worker args (safety-filtered paths)
Detail -> Job: queue DeleteFolders job
note right of Job: FolderDeletionPolicy filters locally and the\nremote script re-checks every path as SYSTEM.

== PumpJobs(): DeleteFolders completes -> CompleteDeleteFolders(job) ==
Detail -> Detail: toast "Cleared N folder(s)"
Detail -> Detail: FindBigFolders("PC-01") (re-scan so the tree\nreflects the freed space)
deactivate Detail
@enduml
